Patchsu patch 8 (optional): incompatible mods made compatible.

Needs 0001 only (no local profiles needed). Also applies together with every other patch (in glob order).

Settings → Patchsu → "Patch 8. Mod compatability": one toggle per normally incompatible mod combination. Off by default,
so nothing changes until a toggle is turned on.

  Hard Rock + Mirror (osu! ruleset): both flips apply. Hard Rock flips vertically, so Mirror on "Vertical" cancels
                                     Hard Rock's flip and "Both" leaves only a horizontal flip. HR's CS/AR/OD/HP
                                     boost and its difficulty/PP effect stay as usual.

Behaviour:
- While a toggle is on, the mod select overlay, presets and the gameplay mod check treat the pair as compatible.
- Turning a toggle off while both mods are selected deselects the second one (Mirror) and keeps Hard Rock.
- Scores/replays using an allowed combination always import, even while its toggle is off.
- Other incompatibilities stay (e.g. Hard Rock + Easy / Difficulty Adjust).

How it works (for later combinations):
- osu.Game/Rulesets/Mods/ModCompatibilityOverrides.cs: the list of combinations (name, hint, setting name, the two mod
  types). A mod's IncompatibleMods leaves out the other mod while ModCompatibilityOverrides.<Pair>.Allowed is true.
  To add one: a new entry in All (its setting is kept in the "ModCompatibility" section of PatchsuSettings.json from
  0001, off by default) and the Allowed check in both mods. HR + MR's value from older builds is taken over from game.ini once.
- OsuGameBase copies each setting into the static Enabled flag and re-checks SelectedMods when one changes.
- ModCompatibilityOverrides.AllowAll() (thread-local scope) is used by ScoreImporter.
- Settings UI: osu.Game/LocalPriority/ModCompatibilitySettings.cs (built from the list). It is a
  PatchSettingsSubsection (from 0001), which Settings → Patchsu finds by itself and sorts by patch number,
  so this patch doesn't edit LocalPrioritySection.

